rubrics_metrics.description:
A singularity model is a nonflat Ricci-flow solution of one of the types:
- Type I model: exists for t∈(−∞,Ω) with 0<Ω<+∞ and satisfies |Rm| ≤ Ω/(Ω−t) everywhere with equality somewhere at t=0;
- Type II model: exists for t∈(−∞,+∞) and satisfies |Rm| ≤ 1 everywhere with equality somewhere at t=0;
- Type III model: exists for t∈(−A,+∞) with 0<A<+∞ and satisfies |Rm| ≤ A/(A+t) everywhere with equality somewhere at t=0.
